WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.450
- Okay, so you know that
taking practice exams

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.500
are important in law school,

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.140
in fact it's one of the
most important things

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.310
that you can do to ensure

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.890
that you get better grades in law school.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:10.290
But there are a lot of subtle things

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.550
that you can do in the way
that you take practice exams

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.030
to maximize their efficiency and ensure

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.550
that you do the best that
you can on your final exam.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.550
So in today's quick tip
we're gonna help you

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:25.130
translate your practice
into reality on your final,

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.302
so stick around.

00:00:26.302 --> 00:00:29.635
(cheerful plucky music)

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.440
A lot of people have trouble
recreating their success

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.420
in practice exams into the classroom

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.990
when their final exam comes around.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.840
The trick is to take practice exams

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.630
under non-ideal conditions.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.620
When you take a practice exam at home,

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.760
it's far too easy to take the exam

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.130
under perfectly ideal conditions,

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.470
to take your practice
exam while you're sitting

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.610
in a really comfortable chair,

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.060
or where your apartment is dead silent

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.960
so it's the perfect time
to take your practice exam,

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.600
or to take it after you've had breakfast

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.340
but before you have lunch,
whenever you feel like it,

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.680
when you feel alert.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.330
But the problem is when you
take your final exam in class

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:19.020
on test day, none of those
conditions will exist.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.360
I guarantee it will
not be perfectly quiet.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.700
You probably won't be sitting
in a comfortable chair,

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.380
it'll be in a hard plastic chair

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.610
with a desk in front of you.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.450
You probably won't have
had a great night's sleep

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.290
because you'll be under so much stress

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:34.560
and you'll be studying right beforehand.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.570
You won't be 10 feet from the refrigerator

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.800
or the bathroom, the clock
is gonna keep running

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.440
regardless of what is
going on in your life.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.470
There are real stakes on the line,

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.830
and that changes everything.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:50.400
But there's a way that we can
turn that to our advantage.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.630
When you take a practice exam at home,

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.713
take it under more stressful situations.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:59.460
Take the exam while there's
music in the background,

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.580
while your roommates are going in and out

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:05.110
from your apartment, when
there's some construction

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.090
on the road in front of you.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:10.350
You can change the conditions
that you get tested under

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.710
to make sure that it's more similar to

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:15.050
how you're going to be
tested on the final exam.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.060
You can make sure that if
you start a practice exam

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.790
you barrel through it and
you don't give yourself

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.310
the crutch of stopping the timer

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.370
to go do something else
and coming back to it.

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:29.570
Go straight through, take
the entire three-hour exam

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:32.010
in one go so that you
don't have the advantage

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.940
of being rested for
every individual section.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.410
It's similar to the story of a famous

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:41.680
Russian Olympic power lifter
who was used to performing

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.230
on his own schedule in a very quiet gym.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.890
He would rest before his lift,

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.950
he would then choose when he'd try to do

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.340
the maximum amount of weight on his lift.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.030
But when he got to the Olympics,

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:56.420
the judges tell you
when you have to perform

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.120
and you only have a few
seconds to go from zero to 60

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.670
to get your job done.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:03.770
In the Olympics you don't
really have a choice,

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:07.680
and it's the same way when
you're taking practice exams.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.360
For example, when I took
the bar exam in California,

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:14.840
in Los Angeles, there was an earthquake

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.890
during the second portion of the bar exam.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.660
Now the bar examiners,
they didn't stop the timer

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:24.300
and I couldn't run under my desk.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.520
I had to barrel through it.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.950
I had to fight all of that adrenaline

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.740
that was running through my
body and just focus on the test.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.730
Luckily it wasn't a huge earthquake,

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.350
but there were a lot of people
who were not from California

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:37.430
who were absolutely freaking out.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.410
Being a native Californian,

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.580
the earthquake wasn't
much of an issue for me

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.160
and I just kept going on, and I feel like

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.340
that gave me an advantage
during the earthquake,

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.540
during the bar exam.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.740
It's the same way during
tests in law school.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.960
If you continually take practice exams

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.600
under ideal conditions,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.750
you are setting yourself up for disaster

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.140
because the real test won't be

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.280
anything like how you practice.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.423
So practice with distracting music.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.960
Take a practice exam with
other people in the room.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.350
Use a timer and don't cheat.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.550
It's far too easy to give
yourself a few extra minutes.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.680
Don't break up the test,

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.250
do the whole thing in one sitting.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:16.830
And find a way to put
real stakes on the line.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.787
The Greek poet Archilochus said,

00:04:18.787 --> 00:04:21.687
"We do not rise to the
level of our expectations,

00:04:21.687 --> 00:04:24.870
"we fall to the level of our training."

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.890
Don't let the conditions
on test day throw you off.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:30.660
Train in ways that are sub-optimal

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.210
so that when you're under
real testing conditions

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.930
you do as well as you possibly can.

